# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, R-4, R-5; the lead's fix 2). L §5.14: "The batch's arrivals are supplies. Parts that arrive at
# x in the same batch are supplies of its takes"; "A movement's take never includes its own arrivals"; a relabel "takes
# parts by the leaving rule and returns them labelled by the arrival rule, batches kept". A relabel's arrival is an
# arrival of its batch, so it is a supply of the batch's other outflows at the place.
# At a batched place the relabel's arrival keeps the batches of its own take, so the place's take reads itself, a
# cycle among the batch's takes; L §5.14.2: "each take is tried with the cycle's arrivals as parts of unknown labels, and
# a take whose outcome is the same under every reading of them ... is decided, which breaks the cycle. Otherwise a cycle
# that holds a plan is refused (RUN-CYCLE, naming the movements) ... A cycle of observed rows only ...: the takes it
# reaches are undecided, each place holds a hole part with its total known".
# The same as observed rows: the takes are undecided, and konto holds a hole part with its total known (60.00;
# scratch/expfix2.py).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
kind lots: place PLN min 0
  batched
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order k.batch.day
kind shifts: transfers
input bank: observed
place konto: lots lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input b1_day: date
input b1_amt: money PLN
input b2_day: date
input b2_amt: money PLN
move b1: transfers
  on b1_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount b1_amt
move b2: transfers
  on b2_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount b2_amt
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-01), bal(konto, 2026-03-01) of b1, bal(konto, 2026-03-01) of b2

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  b1_day = 2026-02-01
  b1_amt = 100.00 PLN
  b2_day = 2026-02-15
  b2_amt = 50.00 PLN
  bank[r] = (on: 2026-03-01, kind: shifts, leg cash from konto to konto amount 30.00 PLN) "r"
  bank[s1] = (on: 2026-03-01, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to shop amount 90.00 PLN) "s1"
=== expect
q: (60.00 PLN, ?"konto: 60.00 PLN may be b1's: which of bank[r], bank[s1] went first on 2026-03-01?" (konto), ?"konto: 60.00 PLN may be b2's: which of bank[r], bank[s1] went first on 2026-03-01?" (konto))
  unfulfilled: b1
  unfulfilled: b2
  cut 2026-10-01
